==English==
[[File:Antonio del pollaiolo, ercole e anteo, 01.JPG|thumb|Heracles girding Antaeus]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ɡɜːd/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɡɝd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-gird.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
{{PIE root|en|gʰerdʰ}}
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|gyrdan||to put a belt around, to put a girdle around}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*gurdijaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*gʰerdʰ-}}. Cognate with Albanian {{m|sq|ngërthej||to tie together by weaving, to bind}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|girds|girding|girded|past2=girt}}

# {{label|en|transitive}} To [[bind]] with a [[flexible]] [[rope]] or [[cord]].
#: ''The fasces were '''girt''' about with twine in bundles large.''
# {{label|en|transitive}} To [[encircle]] with, or as if with a [[belt]].
#: ''The lady '''girt''' herself with silver chain, from which she hung a golden shear.''
#: ''Our home is '''girt''' by sea...'' - [[w:Advance Australia Fair|Advance Australia Fair]]
# {{label|en|transitive}} To [[prepare]] oneself for an [[action]].

